{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: Described in a review: Curr. Protein Pept. Sci. (2020, 21, 527–541). Found in multiple species. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (50%) to frog Dahlein 5.1 A=K: 21%; I=G: 16%. GRAVY: 0.574; mol Wt: 1942.407; mol formula: C91H160N24O22; mol ex coeff: 1490. It has the same aa sequence as LyeTx II. Activity: E. coli (MIC 5-10 uM), S. dysenteriae (MIC 10 uM), S. typhimurium (MIC 5 uM), A. baumannii clinical (MIC 10 uM), P-vulgaris (MIC > 80 uM), P. aeruginosa (MIC 80 uM), Gram+ E. faecium 1359 (MIC 2.5 uM), S. aureus clinical (MIC 5 uM), S-aureus MRSA (MIC>80 uM). In vitro Toxicity: not hemo.lytic at 160 uM; Essentially not toxic to HEK293T, LO2, and 4T1 (cancer cells) at 20 uM. MOA:bacteria: Showed membrane permeabilization E. coli. Structure: became helical in 50% TFE. Est.Jan2024;", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "38276499", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Pharmaceutics. 2024 Jan 19;16(1):129. doi: 10.3390/pharmaceutics16010129. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04051", "source_id": "AP04051", "source_numeric_id": "04051", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04051", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "LC-AMP-F1 Derived from the Venom of the Wolf Spider Lycosa coelestis, Exhibits Antimicrobial and Antibiofilm Activities.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
